    "overviewDetail": "Malaysia is one of Southeast AsiaΓÇÖs most dynamic and diversified economies, strategically positioned along key global trade routes. With a strong foundation in manufacturing, electronics, and oil & gas, the country has evolved into a modern business hub with growing strength in digital services and Islamic finance. Kuala Lumpur acts as the financial and commercial center, supported by world-class infrastructure and a business-friendly regulatory environment.\n\nThe country actively promotes foreign direct investment through incentives in high-growth sectors such as technology, green energy, and advanced manufacturing. Businesses can benefit from relatively straightforward incorporation processes governed by the Companies Commission of Malaysia (SSM), along with competitive tax structures and investment allowances. MalaysiaΓÇÖs participation in regional agreements like RCEP further enhances its position as a gateway to ASEAN markets.\n\nWith a focus on digital transformation and sustainability, Malaysia continues to attract startups, SMEs, and multinational corporations. Its combination of cost efficiency, skilled workforce, and strong connectivity makes it an ideal destination for businesses looking to expand across Asia.\n",
